@startuml
title Workspace vs Cache Security Model

footer
© 2026 Mirko THULKE — All rights reserved
See LICENSE file in the project root for details.
end footer

rectangle "Ephemeral Workspace\n(FLUTTER_CONTAINER_WORKSPACE)" as WS {
  component "git_checkout/"
  component "build/"
  component "android/build/"
  component ".gradle (ephemeral)"
  component "artifacts/"
}

rectangle "Persistent Cache\n(FLUTTER_CONTAINER_CACHE)" as CACHE {
  component ".gradle"
  component ".pub-cache"
  component "flutter/"
}

rectangle "Read-Only Toolchains" as TOOLS {
  component "/opt/flutter"
  component "/opt/rust"
  component "/opt/android/sdk"
}

note right of WS
Writable
Destroyed after build
Safe to clean
No persistent state
end note

note right of CACHE
Writable
Persists across builds
Speeds up dependency resolution
Must NOT contain source code
end note

note right of TOOLS
Read-only
Immutable SDK layer
Protected from modification
Ensures deterministic builds
end note

WS --> CACHE : Uses dependencies
WS --> TOOLS : Uses SDKs
CACHE -[#red]-> TOOLS : No writes allowed

@enduml